(* fs-records-b2s C3-finish, definitional check, (K_s, K_r, T_max) = (2, 1,
   2), any Beacon pins: a Beacon's finish accepts sequence one once.  In this
   scenario the only Server-to-Beacon FsReceived is the one that each Beacon
   session emits at its finish, every Beacon session draws a fresh identity,
   and there is no Beacon receive window (direction split E19), so the
   check holds by construction and is not counted as evidence; its Rust
   reading rests on the pending lifecycle argument L5.  The Server receive
   bound does not reach the Beacon's finish, so it runs at K_r = 1. *)
query s: bitstring, b: bitstring, kid: key_id, root: bitstring, t: nat,
      m1: bitstring, m2: bitstring, i: time, j: time;
  event(FsReceived(server_to_beacon(), s, b, kid, root, t, m1))@i
  && event(FsReceived(server_to_beacon(), s, b, kid, root, t, m2))@j
  ==> i = j.

process FsRecordsB2sMainAnyPin()
